      "description": "For many Jewish Christians of the first century, living in the light of the gospel was challenging. Having accepted Jesus as the long-awaited Messiah, they were regarded by still-skeptical family, friends and neighbors as dangerous, misguided and even disloyal to all that God had said earlier on. The letter to the Hebrews was written to show that you can't go back to an earlier stage of God's purposes but must press on eagerly to the one that is yet to come. In these studies by Tom Wright we find encouragement and assurance that pressing on, even in the face of such close and constant pressure to fall back, is its own reward.\n\nLink to purchase: https://www.amazon.com/Hebrews-Wright-Everyone-Bible-Guides/dp/0830821953/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3QXAHRFZ4UKC2&dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.6jrizCCho3KiaHXvlWSkRM2_Y9JFE2wWP-QbV_AIKNrJ2FBt6-A5RmC24eFTqlv5kfQc9XtoR8woz7_0EjsB2WGhSZeqq9b5N0pQAc5nTEFYAi_nI5aaUKZiyVWeSw7od2FOf1F5rTRP4ElZATBOaqhKBrqiPyq7C7OGAycUeTXf-zlrtTZpcEyGQbYDm_-49lEqatGkbix29Wo_dTs2ecd2ERR6PuFX0PmWUtahBd0.wphhI16Vd4mpN_ibe-aWs0AhJZxhxHgssV0Fdt8bzXY&dib_tag=se&keywords=hebrews+nt+wright&qid=1788559071&sprefix=hebrews+NT,aps,151&sr=8-1",
